# Netlify reads this automatically — no config needed on their end.
# "200" makes these REWRITES (the .html file's content is served, but the
# clean URL stays in the address bar) rather than redirects (which would
# flip the URL back to the messy .html version).
#
# Query strings pass through untouched, so business.html?id=resorts_14
# still works exactly the same as /business?id=resorts_14.

# "/" is left alone on purpose — Netlify already serves index.html there
# by default, which is your landing/splash page, distinct from the app
# home (guest-home.html) people land on after tapping in.

